{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2020",
    "lib": [
      "dom",
      "dom.iterable",
      "esnext"
    ],
    "allowJs": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "strict": false,
    "noEmit": true,
    "incremental": true,
    "module": "esnext",
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    // TS7-MIGRATION D0 — PERMANENT.
    //
    // TypeScript 6.0 stopped INFERRING `rootDir` from the common source
    // directory; it must now be explicit or TS5011 is raised. `tsc -p` never
    // hits this (the include globs span the repo root, so the common source
    // directory is already "."), but ts-jest builds a program per test file,
    // whose common source directory is that file's own folder — so EVERY jest
    // suite failed with TS5011 under TS6 until this was set.
    //
    // "." is the repo root, which is what the `@/*` -> `./*` path map already
    // treats as the source root, and it is what TS6 uses as the new default.
    // Emit layout is unaffected: this project is `noEmit`, and the only
    // emitting project (tsconfig.worker.json) already sets `rootDir: "."`
    // itself, so its output is byte-for-byte unchanged.
    "rootDir": ".",
    // TS7-MIGRATION D0 — TEMPORARY, REMOVE IN D1.
    //
    // TypeScript 6.0 turns `moduleResolution: node10` into a hard error
    // (TS5107), and TWO consumers still request node10:
    //   1. tsconfig.worker.json sets `"moduleResolution": "node"` explicitly.
    //      D1 replaces it with `bundler` (Phase C proved emit-identical).
    //   2. ts-jest forces `moduleResolution: Node10` internally, ignoring this
    //      file entirely (ts-jest 29.4.9 fixupCompilerOptionsForModuleKind).
    //      Without this, EVERY jest suite fails to run under TS6. Fixed
    //      upstream in ts-jest 29.4.12 — not bumped here to keep D0 to a
    //      single-variable change.
    //
    // This ONLY silences the deprecation notice; it changes no resolution,
    // module, or emit semantics. It is inherited by every project that
    // extends this file, so tsconfig.worker.json needs no edit in D0.
    //
    // It buys time, it does not buy a TS7 upgrade. Verified against 7.0.2:
    // the option itself is still ACCEPTED (it becomes a no-op), but node10 is
    // REMOVED outright there — `moduleResolution: node` then fails TS5108 with
    // this option present. So D1 must actually replace node10 with bundler;
    // once it does, delete this line (and prefer ts-jest >= 29.4.12).
    "ignoreDeprecations": "6.0",
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./*"]
    }
  },
  "include": [
    "next-env.d.ts",
    "*.ts",
    "*.tsx",
    "pages/**/*.ts",
    "pages/**/*.tsx",
    "components/**/*.ts",
    "components/**/*.tsx",
    "lib/**/*.ts",
    "lib/**/*.tsx"
  ],
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    ".next",
    "out",
    "docs",
    "tmp",
    "tmp_*",
    "artifacts",
    "backend/tests",
    "supabase/functions",
    "**/*.test.ts",
    "**/*.spec.ts",
  ]
}
